1. Parse the events and identify segments between type 1 events
2. Build a conflict graph where edges connect friends who appear together in any segment
3. Find the maximum independent set (maximum number of non-conflicting friends)

Key insight: Friends who visit in the same segment cannot both be happy (since only one handle can be set per segment). So we need to find the maximum set of friends where no two friends ever appear in the same segment.

```python
import sys
